window.docContents[172].resolve({"/The-Coleman-map/#An-introduction-to-p-adic-L-functions-___-Lean-blueprint--The-Coleman-map":{"contents":"Throughout this chapter  is an odd prime and we work with coefficient field\n. We bring the arithmetic of cyclotomic fields into the picture through the\ntheory of local units. The main result is a theorem of Coleman identifying\nnorm-coherent systems of local units with a distinguished space of power series\nover ; under the Mahler transform these become -adic measures. Applied to\ncyclotomic units, this machinery reconstructs the Kubota–Leopoldt -adic\n-function  on the algebraic side, packaged as the Coleman map.\nThis is the key bridge between the analytic object  and arithmetic, and is\nthe first step towards the Iwasawa Main Conjecture. See \nfor Coleman's original work and  for the treatment we\nfollow.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"An introduction to p-adic L-functions — Lean blueprint","header":"9. The Coleman map","id":"/The-Coleman-map/#An-introduction-to-p-adic-L-functions-___-Lean-blueprint--The-Coleman-map"}});